    "question": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 220\" style=\"max-width:520px; margin:0.8em auto; display:block;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n  <defs>\n    <marker id=\"utd\" markerWidth=\"10\" markerHeight=\"7\" refX=\"0\" refY=\"3.5\" orient=\"auto\">\n      <polygon points=\"0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7\" fill=\"#1e3a8a\"/>\n    </marker>\n    <marker id=\"utu\" markerWidth=\"10\" markerHeight=\"7\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"3.5\" orient=\"auto\">\n      <polygon points=\"10 0, 0 3.5, 10 7\" fill=\"#b91c1c\"/>\n    </marker>\n  </defs>\n  <!-- Fluid tank background -->\n  <rect x=\"100\" y=\"30\" width=\"400\" height=\"170\" fill=\"#1e90ff\" fill-opacity=\"0.2\" stroke=\"#475569\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"6\"/>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1e90ff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-family=\"'Source Serif 4',serif\">water</text>\n  <!-- Object (cube) -->\n  <rect x=\"245\" y=\"95\" width=\"110\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#1e3a8a\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"4\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"white\" font-family=\"'Source Serif 4',serif\">V = 0.18 m³</text>\n  <!-- Weight arrow down -->\n  <line x1=\"260\" y1=\"175\" x2=\"260\" y2=\"205\" stroke=\"#1e3a8a\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#utd)\"/>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1e3a8a\" font-family=\"'Source Serif 4',serif\">W = 1800 N</text>\n  <!-- Upthrust arrow up -->\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"175\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"58\" stroke=\"#b91c1c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#utu)\"/>\n  <text x=\"348\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#b91c1c\" font-family=\"'Source Serif 4',serif\">Upthrust</text>\n  <text x=\"348\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#b91c1c\" font-family=\"'Source Serif 4',serif\">= ?</text>\n</svg><p style=\"margin-top:0.8em;\">A block weighing 1800 N floats on water with 60% of its volume submerged. If the submerged volume is 0.18 m³, verify that the upthrust equals the weight. (Density of water = 1000 kg/m³, g = 10 N/kg) Calculate the upthrust.</p>",
